{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_check.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nclaim='C-storage-qualified-commit'\nbinding='D-commit-aggregation'\nsources=[dict(id='durability-expectation',file='raft.go',start_line=550,end_line=576,kind='document_statement'),dict(id='bootstrap-contract',file='bootstrap.go',start_line=23,end_line=80,kind='code_observation')]\nground=dict(source_ids=['reply-queue','reset-append','leader-match','tracker-commit','majority','log-eligibility'],expectation_ids=['durability-expectation','async-contract'],binding_ids=[binding],derivation='The implementation explicitly requires entries to be persisted before being counted toward commitment (durability-expectation). The async contract permits outgoing replication before local writes but requires storage-worker responses after ordered durable completion. Under a fixed simple voting configuration, commitment may use any majority of persisted matching replicas; it does not require the leader itself to have persisted when other replicas form a majority. This requirement is independent of the observed committed value and of a blanket expectation that delayed local writes block every commit.',applicability='Non-Byzantine peers; stable fixed simple voter membership; async storage mode; current-term ordinary proposal; honest ordered storage workers, no crashes or data corruption. MemoryStorage represents successfully completed storage writes at the library boundary; no physical disk durability is measured.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['A three-voter leader may legally commit using both followers while its own append worker is delayed.'])\nquestion=dict(question='Can leader commitment of a current-term proposal advance before the replicas whose storage workers have completed matching appends constitute the active voting majority, when the leader append worker is finitely delayed?',importance='Counting an undurable replica toward a required majority can expose committed data to loss after failures. The proposed check observes only the library commitment boundary and storage completion ordering, not crash-induced data loss or client completion.',source_ids=['durability-expectation','async-contract','reset-append','leader-match','tracker-commit','majority','log-eligibility'],participants=['Leader and non-Byzantine voting followers','Serialized RawNode callers and FIFO local append/apply workers'],objects=['Current-term log entry','Leader committed prefix','Per-voter stored log and Match'],contexts=['AsyncStorageWrites with fixed simple voter membership','Leader append worker held while remote append workers and messages run, then released'],event_paths=['RawNode.Propose -> appendEntry -> deferred self MsgAppResp / remote MsgApp -> follower append -> storage response -> leader Match -> majority -> maybeCommit'],activity_classes=['A1'],behavior_ids=['B-aggregate','B-apply'],fact_ids=['F-committed'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-propose':'Produces the current-term target entry and deferred self append response.','B-follower-append':'Actual remote producer of append acknowledgements.','B-storage-release':'A6 handoff constrains when remote and local acknowledgement support becomes consumable by A1.','B-election-result':'Actual election establishes the tested leader, avoiding direct role assignment.','B-membership':'Bootstrap and application establish the fixed voter identities used by the oracle.','B-entry':'RawNode is serialized and the driver implements asynchronous caller duties.'},obligation_relation_kind='establishment',counterevidence=['send queues self and remote append responses in msgsAfterAppend.','Async Ready envelopes defer these responses until local append completion.','maybeCommit requires a current-term entry and tracker aggregates only active voters.','A follower majority without the leader is legitimate, so local persistence is not an unconditional prerequisite.'],unknowns=['Whether actual self and remote producers, asynchronous Ready collection and commitment consumer preserve the storage-qualified quorum relation in a complete finite execution with held leader writes.'],priority=3,trigger_rationale='The source separates sending replication from publishing support, and initializes self Match during role transitions. A real elected leader and proposal with delayed local appends tests this distinction at the commit endpoint. Two voters make the leader necessary; three voters supply a permitted follower-majority control.',disposition='ready_for_check',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\nobligation=dict(id=claim,kind='obligation',concern='consensus_safety',description='Under a fixed simple voter configuration and compliant asynchronous storage workers, a leader may count replicas toward commitment of a current-term entry only after matching log entries have completed storage writes on those replicas; an advanced committed prefix must therefore be backed by a voting majority of such replicas.',source_ids=['durability-expectation','async-contract','majority','log-eligibility'],scope=dict(description='Storage-qualified leader commitment of ordinary current-term entries in fixed simple configurations under asynchronous Ready processing.',assumptions=['Non-Byzantine messages and honest FIFO storage workers.','No membership changes during the selected proposal interval.','MemoryStorage is the storage-completion model; completed writes are not lost during these executions.'],excluded=['Physical disk durability and crash recovery','Joint configurations and dynamic membership','Byzantine or forged messages','Global consensus safety or client linearizability conclusions'],parameters={'async_storage_writes':True,'configuration':'fixed simple voters'}),pending=[],grounding=ground)\nbind=dict(id=binding,material_id='reset-append',symbol='maybeCommit',start_line=778,end_line=782,description='Leader combines current term with tracker quorum index before raftLog commitment.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim,source_ids=['durability-expectation','async-contract','tracker-commit','majority','log-eligibility'],rationale='This consumer is the commitment endpoint for queued storage-qualified append support.')])\ncandidate=dict(action='obligation',rationale='Test an explicit persistence-before-counting responsibility without assuming local leader persistence is always necessary.',question=question,obligation=obligation,bindings=[bind])\nlegality=dict(source_ids=['entry','bootstrap-contract','async-contract','storage-memory','storage-snap-append','candidate-follower','campaign','apply-accept','storage-envelope','storage-tail'],expectation_ids=['async-contract','conf-contract'],binding_ids=[binding],derivation='Create each RawNode with MemoryStorage and Bootstrap identical peers; drain bootstrap entries and invoke ApplyConfChange only on emitted committed configuration entries. Campaign through the public method and deliver actual produced messages until a leader emerges. Propose through RawNode; no term, role, log, tracker or commit assignments occur. Each local append queue processes FIFO and publishes carried responses only after writes. Apply queues are independently FIFO and consume real entries; public Step receives actual produced responses. After the proposal only the leader append worker is finitely held, which async-contract permits while other workers run; all held work is subsequently released. No Advance is called in async mode. The loop stops on lack of eligible work or a driver budget independently of the forbidden commitment predicate.',applicability='Two separate clusters with two and three voters, no post-bootstrap configuration changes, no crashes, drops or ticks during the selected interval. The finite drain budget is a driver limit, not a liveness conclusion.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Synchronous Ready has different caller ordering, so this driver is restricted to the async public API.'])\nplan=dict(description='Elect a leader from public Bootstrap/Campaign in two- and three-voter clusters, propose one unique payload per cluster, drain all eligible work with the leader append worker held, observe commitment against matching stored replica count, release that worker and drain again. The three-voter held phase exercises a permitted follower-majority commit; final scenario events report committed and applied endpoints. Each observation has an independent scenario/phase ID emitted before its schedule.',claim_id=claim,binding_ids=[binding],harness=dict(kind='go_test',source='',files={},description='Serialized public RawNode driver with deterministic FIFO local storage workers and in-memory network. Four finite checkpoint operations over two complete proposal histories.',semantic_changes=['No implementation modifications; same-package access reads target index, self Match and applied index only.','MemoryStorage substitutes for durable backend completion. No crash recovery or filesystem durability claim.','Derived booleans compare raw leader commit >= target index and matching persisted replica count >= configured majority. Raw operands are emitted.'],prerequisites=[dict(alias='admission',event='admitted',conditions=[dict(field='proposal_admitted',op='eq',value=True)])],legality=legality),monitors=[dict(id='M-storage-qualified-commit',checker_id='storage-qualified-commit',event='checkpoint',binding_ids=[binding],grounding=ground,admission_alias='admission',applicability_conditions=[])],observable_properties=[dict(checker_id='storage-qualified-commit',kind='event_implication',trigger=dict(field='schedule_complete',op='eq',value=True),antecedent=dict(field='committed_target',op='eq',value=True),assertion=dict(field='storage_quorum',op='eq',value=True),identity_fields=['observation_id'],description='At each completed scheduled checkpoint, commitment of the target implies a majority of independently inspected MemoryStorage replicas contain the targe